  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Cefotetan is a cephalosporin antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections such as sepsis, abscesses, urinary tract infections, peritonitis, and gram-negative or staphylococcal infections. It is an approved antibiotic, though it does not appear to be authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2602246&quot;>Wikidata Q2602246</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>cefotetan</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J01DC05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01330&quot;>DB01330</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/53025&quot;>53025</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:3499&quot;>3499</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2602246&quot;>Q2602246</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C17H17N7O8S4</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>575.604 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
